  "id": "panthi_satnami",
  "name": "Panthi (Satnami devotional song-dance)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Panthi is the devotional song-dance of the Satnami community of Chhattisgarh, performed in praise of Guru Ghasidas, the founder of the Satnami sect, especially around his birth anniversary. Male dancers sing his teachings in a circle to the mandar barrel drum and the jhanjh cymbals as the tempo builds to a fast climax; here a generic membrane drum card stands in for the mandar. Devdas Banjare took Panthi to stages across India and abroad.",
  "recipe": "classic modern panthi, praise Song, indian subcontinent branch. membrane drum pulse resonant acoustic membrane drum, credited cymbals. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
